A||N||13||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||Have you seen Spiral Max? Think it Works?||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||04-30-2000||03:58 AM||||<BR>Have you guys or gals, seen Spiral Max?  If you haven't go to <A HREF="http://www.spiralmax.com" TARGET=_blank>www.spiralmax.com</A>  .  What do you think?  Do you think it could work?  Or is it a waste of money?  But still it is only $69.95, if even a 5hp increase would be worth it, if you didn't get the up to 35hp they claim.  Opinions?    ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ozzy||04-30-2000||04:12 AM||||I've seen this before...theory sounds good but Fiero's are not amongst the list of applications in the Pontiac line. The theory is spinning or swirling air turns corners easier improving airflow thru head intake chambers. I would think something like this would be easy to make and place in the air intake duct...what improvements??? I've heard someone say real horsepower is not cheap? <P>2 b honest, I don't know if it works or not but depends what kinda budget you got to play with. It is not really a lot of money.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||04-30-2000||04:49 AM||||I can get you a fantastic deal on some beach front property thats not far from where I live.<P>Mike B.||||reg||7
Z||000003||Oreif||04-30-2000||09:21 AM||||I've been to the spiralmax website and on a different message board they had a discussion of it. The overall agreement was, 1 spiralmax = 15hp 2 one at each end of the hose = 30hp and the coffee can exhaust tube was another 10hp. Also if you removed the Fiero rubber inlet tube and replaced it with a chrome one that added another 15hp. Also Also spralmax has this bridge........   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Actually spiralmax "claims" HP gains but it never has been actaully proven by someone else. I've read the letters people have written in praise of them but I think they are "a$$-O-meter" results. In reality I think you may get a gallon or 2 increase in gas milage due to the spiral effect but as for true HP I doubt it. The spiralmax will fit any car its just a bladed piece of stainless steel to swirl the air.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||04-30-2000||10:37 AM||||In my opinion it will have no measureable positive benefit.  Dyno testing has shown that the Fiero intake system is not a limiting factor on a stock or moderately modified Fiero engine.  Even taking out the restrictions in the air box has shown no benefit.<P>Theories like those that support Spiralmax usually have basic flaws that sound great to the layman.  I think that if it was a great idea one of the major manufacturers or race engine designers would jump on it.  I don't see that with Spiralmax.<P>I wouldn't waste my money.||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||04-30-2000||11:03 AM||||I think you'll get the same benefit by going to Wal-Mart, buying a plastic kid's pinwheel and duct taping it next to your air intake. This way, you've got $59.60 left to buy gas with.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spyder||04-30-2000||11:28 AM||||<BR>Yep, what they said and I don’t believe it would be worth it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||04-30-2000||12:22 PM||||isn't that in the new VTECH motor?  ahhemmm....<P>honda gained 30 hp from a spinning thing in their intake that acts like a supercharger but is a lot less money.<P>I'll look it up sometime because if honda uses it and claims HP then it most likely works.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||04-30-2000||01:08 PM||||Consumer Reports tested a similar gimmick on two vehicles, it was called the Tornado and it did nothing to one vehicle and cost the other 5 HP. Save your money and read this. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt</A>   It’s a very good article about what to modify on the fiero 2.8 and what to leave alone.<P>Consumer Reports if you don't know is a nonprofit organization that is not influenced by advertising in its magazine because there is non. It's a very reliable sorce of information about the truth on products like the Tornado.<P>Don't be a sucker!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||04-30-2000||02:32 PM||||I'd be interested to see what Ogre has to say about the Spiral Max.... Teehee||||reg||10
Z||000010||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||05-01-2000||01:32 AM||||I was just asking because sometimes people do come out with new products that work.  Think of the poor fool that thought Turbos was some gimick.  I asked here, for that reason that is all.  If believed everything I read I would have just went out and bought it.  But thanks for the info.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Jeff's '86 1/2 GT (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||05-01-2000||02:42 PM||||wouldn't waste the money.. for the same idea and REAL gain...  <A HREF="http://www.electricsupercharger.com" TARGET=_blank>www.electricsupercharger.com</A>    it works!||||reg||1
Z||000012||mshill||05-01-2000||04:12 PM||||What they said... and even if you got 2 more mpg it is going to take you 9K miles to pay for itself (longer when gas prices come down).  That's probably great if you drive your fiero 10-15K miles a year.  I doubt I will put over 4K a year on mine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||05-01-2000||04:34 PM||||Well I have 285,000 miles on th car since bought new in July of 1986. Same enigine, with no smoke, and great oil pressure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So I guess that means that I am putting on a little over 20,000 miles a year on the car.  Guess I could have it paid off in 6 months. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
